# Define the complete GT machine tooltip here so stale GregTech language configs cannot hide newer mod text.
gt.blockmachines.fissionevolved.fission_reactor_controller.tooltip=Machine Type: §eLarge Fission Reactor§r\n§aSupports native GTNH and addon GT nuclear fuel rods\nBase output per rod: §eoriginal pulse output x 900§7 x §dfuel characteristic multiplier\nRun time: §f1/1000 of original durability§7, minimum §f1 second\nCasing parallel: §664 to 8192§7; every coil tier grants §dx2 generation\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\n§cConsumes all fuel rods at startup§7; each run processes one fuel type\nOn completion, §adirectly outputs§7 depleted-rod processing products\n§cWarning:§7 manual shutdown or structural failure loses committed fuel and pending outputs\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nConsume §9coolants§7 to increase §dgeneration§7:\n§f1000 L/s§7: §d125%§7: §9Water\n§f1000 L/s§7: §d150%§7: §9Distilled Water\n§f1000 L/s§7: §d200%§7: §9IC2 Coolant\n§f1000 L/s§7: §d400%§7: §9Super Coolant\n§f1000 L/s§7: §d800%§7: §9Cryotheum\n§f20 L/s§7: §d1600%§7: §9Tachyon Rich Temporal Fluid\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\n§aSupports standard, multi-amp, wireless, and laser dynamo hatches!\nPower enters the §econtroller buffer§7 first; low hatch throughput §acannot cause explosions\nA full buffer §6pauses automatically§7 without consuming fuel life or coolant\nWireless output can be toggled in the GUI or with a screwdriver; §cdisabled by default\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\n§7Added by: §6Fission Evolved§r\nHold §l[LSHIFT]§r§7 to display structure guidance
gt.blockmachines.fissionevolved.fission_reactor_controller.tooltip_secondary=§fDimensions: §67§7x§67§7x§67 (§6L§7x§6W§7x§6H§7) \n§fStructure: \n   §fController: §7Front center\n   §6112 §fMatching Metal Machine Casings §7(frame and reflector; frame is hatch-replaceable)\n   §6149 §fMatching Tiered Glass §7(hatch-replaceable)\n   §627 §fMatching Heating Coils\n   §e1+ §fItem Input Bus: §7Any outer frame or glass position\n   §e1+ §fItem Output Bus: §7Any outer frame or glass position\n   §e0+ §fFluid Input Hatch: §7Any outer frame or glass position\n   §e0+ §fFluid Output Hatch: §7Any outer frame or glass position\n   §e1+ §fDynamo Hatch: §7Any outer frame or glass position\n   §e0+ §fMaintenance Hatch: §7Any outer frame or glass position\n   No hatch limit; supports standard, multi-amp, wireless, and laser dynamos\n   The frame and reflector share one casing tier; glass and coils each use one matching tier\n   \nUse §bcasing§7 to select the casing tier\nUse §bcoil§7 to select the coil tier\nUse §bglass§7 to select the glass tier\n§7§m------------------------------\n§fUse a multiblock §9hologram projector§f to view or construct the complete structure!
gt.blockmachines.fissionevolved.colossal_fission_reactor_controller.tooltip=Machine Type: §eUltimate Universe-Destroying Generator§r\n§dBig! Strong! Ridiculous amounts of power!\n§f48x48x32 §7chunk-scale endgame power structure\n§dExclusive fuels: Eternal Entropy Ember, Omniversal Stellar Core, Spacetime Devourer, and Primordial Godblight\nPer-rod base generation: §e10^30 / 10^40 / 10^50 / 10^60 EU/t\nEach run lasts §f1 hour§7 by default\nA §6TST Proof of Heroes§7 in the controller slot extends it to §f24 hours§7 and is §anot consumed\nTier 3/6/9 structures multiply final generation by §dx1 / x5 / x10\n§6Maximum parallel: 1,048,576§7 (unaffected by structure tier)\nFuel is §cconsumed at startup§7; §ano items or fluids are produced\n§bNo dynamo hatch required; power goes directly to the wireless EU network\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\n§7Added by: §6Fission Evolved§r\nHold §l[LSHIFT]§r§7 to display structure guidance
gt.blockmachines.fissionevolved.colossal_fission_reactor_controller.tooltip_secondary=§fDimensions: §648§7x§648§7x§632§7 (§6L§7x§6W§7x§6H§7) \n§fStructure: \n   §fController: §7Front center\n   §fFission Reactor Containment Casing: §7stepped octagonal vessel\n   §fMatching Tiered Glass: §7outer windows\n   §fNeutron Reflector Matrices and Fission Core Energy Conduits: §7inner core\n   §fSpacetime Compression, Stabilisation, and Time Acceleration Fields: §btier 3/6/9 only, all matching\n   §aForms with zero hatches; §7hatches remain optional on casing and glass positions\n   §bUnmarked interior positions are completely ignored, §7so automation may be placed there\n   \nUse §bspacetime_compression§7 to select the compression field tier\nUse §bstabilisation§7 to select the stabilisation field tier\nUse §btime_dilation§7 to select the time field tier\nUse §bglass§7 to select the glass tier\n§7§m------------------------------\n§fUse a multiblock §9hologram projector§f to view or construct the complete structure!
